Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: coral-usb-hwmon-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms
Suggests: lm-sensors
Description: Temperature monitoring for the Google Coral USB Accelerator
 Exposes the on-chip sensor via Linux hwmon. An optional apex compatibility
 class supplies the temperature path used by Frigate on USB-only systems.
 DKMS builds the module using the headers for each target kernel.

Package: coral-usb-tools
Architecture: linux-any
Section: utils
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: USB diagnostics for the Google Coral USB Accelerator
 Reads the configured TPU clock, temperature sensor and USB fatal interrupt
 flag from an initialized accelerator. Can capture a timestamped status
 sample while an Edge TPU application is running.
